#X obj 660 8 seq.toggles;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 421 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Toggle sequencer: outputs 1 when an event starts and
0 when it ends. The pattern is given in beat duration units (relative
to @t) \, and the duration of each event is controlled by @length.
This makes it convenient for driving gates \, envelopes or any object
that expects an on/off control signal.;
#X text 240 184 Event length (@length) can be specified in three forms:;
#X text 250 209 • percent: @length 60% with @t 100ms — for an event
value of 2 (duration 200ms) \, the event length will be 120ms.;
#X text 250 264 • fixed: @length 10 or @length 10ms with @t 100ms —
the event length is fixed at 10ms regardless of how long the event
lasts.;
#X text 250 319 • subtract: @length -40 with @t 100ms — for an event
value of 2 (duration 200ms) \, the event length is 160ms (200−40) \,
for an event value of 1 (duration 100ms) \, the event length is 60ms
(100−40).;
#X text 240 389 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 414 • Gate patterns for envelopes — driving the gate input
of an envelope generator (for example \, [env.adsr~]) with rhythmic
on/off events \, so that each note has the correct attack and release
behaviour.;
